pelican-egg-dune-awakening
==========================

This project ports CubeCoders' AMP module for Dune: Awakening to
Pelican / Wings.

The contents of the `scripts/` directory (all `*.sh` files and
`templates/director.ini`) were originally copied from CubeCoders' upstream
AMPTemplates and have since been forked with modifications for Pelican
Wings (stripped AMP daemon assumptions, dropped customstart.sh, added
phased shutdown grace periods, Funcom DB migration regression
workarounds, etc.). See ATTRIBUTION.md for details.

Original source: https://github.com/CubeCoders/AMPTemplates
Original license: MIT, Copyright (c) 2024 CubeCoders Limited
See LICENSE for the full grant.

`mock-k8s/` is an open-source Go re-implementation of the Kubernetes API
mock that the Battlegroup Director talks to. The original closed binary
shipped by CubeCoders refused to run outside AMP (anti-tamper check),
so we wrote our own from scratch and ship its source — MIT-licensed,
built deterministically at install time. See ATTRIBUTION.md.

`scripts/pelican-entrypoint.sh` and `scripts/apply-config.sh` are this
fork's own contributions, also MIT-licensed.

Modifications, additions, and the Pelican egg JSON itself are by
valentin95150@hotmail.fr and contributors, and are also released under MIT.

Funcom owns and distributes the underlying Dune: Awakening dedicated server
binaries. This project does not redistribute Funcom's binaries — they are
fetched on demand from Steam via SteamCMD's anonymous public depot mode at
egg-install time. Operators are responsible for complying with Funcom's
end-user license agreement and self-host server terms.

